g_wm="""<h2>How to watermark a PDF</h2><ol><li>Choose one or more PDF files.</li><li>Type the watermark text, for example <i>DRAFT</i>, <i>CONFIDENTIAL</i> or <i>BẢN NHÁP – 社外秘</i>, or switch to <b>Image</b> and choose a PNG or JPG logo.</li><li>Pick the placement: center, tiled across the page, or one of nine positions. Set the rotation, opacity, size and color.</li><li>Optionally limit the pages (for example <code>1-3, 5</code>), click <b>Add watermark</b> and download the PDF, or a ZIP when you chose several files.</li></ol>
<h2>How it works</h2><p>The watermark is added as real vector text or as one embedded image on top of each page; the pages are not turned into pictures, so the original text stays sharp, selectable and searchable. The tool reads each page as you see it on screen: it uses the visible area (crop box) and follows pages rotated by 90°, 180° or 270°, so a diagonal watermark is centered and upright on portrait, landscape and mixed-size pages. If the text would not fit, it is made smaller automatically.</p><p>Text is drawn with the embedded Noto Sans and Noto Sans JP fonts, so Vietnamese accents and Japanese characters display correctly. Only the characters you use are embedded, once per file, and the image is stored once and reused on every page, so even a 120-page file grows by only a few kilobytes plus the image size. Characters the fonts cannot draw, such as emoji, are reported instead of being replaced with boxes.</p>
<h2>Settings explained</h2><ul><li><b>Size</b> is a percentage of the visible page width, so the watermark looks the same on A4, Letter and A3 pages.</li><li><b>Opacity</b> only affects the watermark; your page content is not faded. 100 % is fully solid.</li><li><b>Rotation</b> accepts −360 to 360 degrees; 45 is the classic diagonal, 360 is the same as 0.</li><li><b>Tiled</b> repeats the watermark in an even grid centered on the page, so the cut edges are the same on both sides.</li></ul>
<h2>Good to know</h2><ul><li>Password-protected or permission-restricted PDFs are not changed. Open them in <a href='/unlock-pdf/'>Unlock PDF</a> first (you need the right to do so), then add the watermark.</li><li>Digitally signed PDFs: any change invalidates the signature, so the tool warns you before you download.</li><li>Links, bookmarks, form fields and the document title and author are kept. Form fields stay fillable because they sit above the page content.</li><li>To add page numbers, a header or a logo in a corner, use <a href='/add-page-numbers-to-pdf/'>Add Page Numbers to PDF</a>.</li></ul>
"""+FAQ2(("Can a watermark be removed?","Yes. A watermark discourages copying and marks a document as a draft or confidential, but anyone with a PDF editor can delete it. It is not copy protection or DRM."),("Can the watermark text be copied or searched?","Yes. Text watermarks are real text, so they appear when someone copies the page text or searches the PDF. Use an image watermark if you do not want that."),("Are my PDFs uploaded?","No. The watermark is added inside your browser with the pdf-lib library. Your files, the watermark text and the image never leave your device and are not stored."),("What happens with password-protected PDFs?","Files with an open password or with permission restrictions (owner password) are not processed, so you never get a damaged or silently unlocked file. Remove the protection with Unlock PDF first if you are allowed to."),("Will the file get much bigger?","Usually only by a few kilobytes, because the font subset and the image are embedded once per file and reused on every page."))
