g_dr="""<h2>How to remove duplicate rows</h2><ol><li>Choose a CSV, TSV or Excel file. A preview of the first rows appears.</li><li>Compare by all columns, or choose key columns such as <i>Email</i>, or <i>Name</i> + <i>Phone</i>.</li><li>Pick the matching options and whether to keep the first or the last copy, then click <b>Remove duplicates</b>.</li><li>Download the cleaned file and, if you want to check, the file with the removed duplicates.</li></ol>
<h2>How rows are compared</h2><p>Two rows are duplicates when the compared cells are equal as text after the options you tick:</p><ul><li><b>Spaces at the start and end</b> are ignored, including non-breaking spaces and the Japanese full-width space, and tabs.</li><li><b>Several spaces inside a cell</b> can count as one, so "Nguyễn  Văn" equals "Nguyễn Văn".</li><li><b>Upper/lower case</b> can be ignored, also for Vietnamese letters: "ĐẠT" equals "đạt".</li><li><b>Unicode NFC</b> treats a letter typed as one character or as a letter plus accent (common in files from Mac or some web forms) as the same.</li><li><b>NFKC</b> also treats full-width "ＡＢＣ" and half-width "ABC", or full-width and half-width katakana, as the same. It is off by default.</li></ul><p>Values are compared as text: "0912345678" and "912345678" differ, and so do "1.0" and "1". A cell with a line break inside quotes counts as one cell.</p><p>These options are only used to compare. The cleaned file keeps your original values (for example "Nguyễn " with its trailing space) unless you tick <b>Also clean the kept rows</b>.</p>
<h2>Which copy is kept</h2><p><b>Keep the first copy</b> keeps the earliest row and removes later ones; <b>Keep the last copy</b> keeps the latest row, for example the most recent update of a customer. Kept rows stay in their original order. Empty rows can be removed and are counted separately, not as duplicates.</p>
<h2>Files and output</h2><p>The same encoding and delimiter detection as <a href='/merge-csv/'>Merge CSV &amp; Excel Files</a> is used: UTF-8 and UTF-16 automatically, Windows-1252, Windows-1258 and Shift_JIS on request. Output is CSV (UTF-8 with BOM) or XLSX with IDs and leading zeros kept as text. Large files of 200,000 rows or more run in a background worker with a progress bar. To convert between CSV and Excel without removing anything, use <a href='/csv-to-excel/'>CSV to Excel</a>.</p>
"""+FAQ2(("Is my file uploaded?","No. Everything runs in your browser and the tool works offline once the page has loaded. Nothing is sent to a server or saved."),("Why were fewer duplicates found than I expected?","Values must match exactly as text after the options you choose. Try ignoring upper/lower case, extra spaces or full-width characters, or compare only the key columns such as Email."),("Can I see which rows were removed?","Yes. Download the second file: it contains every removed duplicate with the header."),("Does it count the header row?","No. The counts show data rows only. Untick “The first row is a header” if your file has no header."),("Is it safe to open the result in Excel?","Yes. Cells that start with = + - or @ get a leading apostrophe in CSV output so they do not run as formulas, and XLSX output stores them as text."))
add2("remove-duplicate-rows","Spreadsheet tools","Remove Duplicate Rows","Remove Duplicate Rows from CSV & Excel – Free, No Upload","Remove duplicate rows from CSV or Excel files in your browser: compare all or chosen columns, ignore case and spaces, keep the first or last copy, and download the removed rows too.",ui_dr,js_dr,g_dr)
